          "label": null,
          "section": "6.2.2",
          "printed_page": "230",
          "pdf_page": "251",
          "statement_latex": "In contrast, the Stratonovich (midpoint) integral can be calculated as\n\\[\\int_0^\\tau W(t)\\circ dW(t)=\\operatorname{l.i.m.}_{\\nu\\to\\infty}\\sum_{k=0}^{\\nu-1}W(k\\delta t+\\delta t/2)[W((k+1)\\delta t)-W(k\\delta t)].\\]\nWriting\n\\[W(k\\delta t+\\delta t/2)=W(\\frac{(k+1)\\delta t+k\\delta t}{2})=\\frac12(W((k+1)\\delta t)+W(k\\delta t))+O(\\sqrt{\\delta t}),\\]\nallows us to evaluate the integral as\n\\[\\int_0^\\tau W(t)\\circ dW(t)=\\frac12\\operatorname{l.i.m.}_{\\nu\\to\\infty}\\sum_{k=0}^{\\nu-1}[W((k+1)\\delta t)^2-W(k\\delta t)^2]=\\frac12W(\\tau)^2.\\]",
          "proof_latex": null,
          "proof_note": "原书未给独立完整证明。",
          "proof_discussion_latex": null,
          "context_notation": [],
